# Flare .gitignore
# Stack-agnostic baseline. The stack is not chosen yet: add its rules (dependencies,
# build output, virtual environments) BEFORE anyone installs anything.
#
# Deliberately NOT ignored, do not add broad patterns for these:
#   - simulated seed data and the labelled RO/EN test set (*.json, *.csv, ...)
#   - .env.example
#   - lockfiles
# Ignoring does not protect files that are already tracked or already in history.
# If a secret is ever committed, rotate it.

# --- Secrets ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
credentials.json
service-account*.json

# --- Personal Claude Code config (the shared .claude/settings.json IS committed) ---
.claude/settings.local.json

# --- Real passenger data: never commit (demo uses simulated data only) ---
uploads/
photos/

# --- Local databases and logs ---
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.log

# --- Demo fallback recording (large; share outside git) ---
/recordings/

# --- Temp and scratch ---
tmp/
temp/
*.tmp
*.swp

# --- OS and editor ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.vscode/
.idea/
